SCP-firmware v2.11.0's dvfs module with CIX's changes to it:
- the configuration fields CIX added (reference_perf_level, the level
  reported for the sustained OPP; opp_level_num, the OPPs in use), filled
  in by the configuration;
- dvfs_get_sustained_opp answers FWK_E_RANGE when the sustained index is
  outside the table, and dvfs_start leaves such a domain alone (upstream:
  FWK_E_PARAM, and the start fails);
- when the new OPP has the voltage of the current one, the frequency is
  set anyway (upstream: only while no frequency has been set yet);
- a request whose cookie is sky1soc_perf's module identifier is reported
  to that module (event MOD_SKY1SOC_PERF_EVENT_IDX_DVFS_DONE) when it
  completes, whatever the outcome.
Everything else is upstream's (BSD-3-Clause, see
../../../SCP-firmware/license.md).
